From 06bcdf3d6f26160908494c1333e9b0c3ad573e23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:20:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dashboard): exempt loopback control-read from
 session-token path scan [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem: PR #3757 CI shard 3/6 failed on 31af0181d7ff:
test_every_session_header_caller_targets_a_session_token_route — _loopback_control_get
sends X-Hermes-Session-Token but its target path could not be read.

Why 1: The scanner requires a literal /api/... in the function, or an _EXEMPT entry.
Why 2: The path is a parameter (CONTROL_READ_PATHS), same as _http_get.
Why 3: Registering /api/model/options as a session-token route would widen the gated
dashboard cookie gate — out of scope and the wrong trust boundary.
Root: loopback always-on backends are serve --isolated on 127.0.0.1, never gated;
_http_get/_http_post already carry that exemption.

Countermeasures:
- symptom: add _loopback_control_get to _EXEMPT next to _http_get.
- root: do not register control-read paths as SESSION_TOKEN_SERVICE_ROUTES.
- detection: test_dashboard_session_token_routes.py (the failing CI test).

Proof: hermes-core-wt test of test_dashboard_session_token_routes.py and
test_always_on_control_handoff.py — 21 passed.
---
 hermes_cli/always_on_rollover.py                        | 2 ++
 tests/hermes_cli/test_dashboard_session_token_routes.py | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hermes_cli/always_on_rollover.py b/hermes_cli/always_on_rollover.py
index 71479810b2..906b8a70f0 100644
--- a/hermes_cli/always_on_rollover.py
+++ b/hermes_cli/always_on_rollover.py
@@ -181,6 +181,8 @@ def handoff_control_read(port: int, path: str, *, get: Optional[Callable] = None
 
 
 def _loopback_control_get(port: int, path: str, timeout: float) -> tuple[Optional[int], float, Optional[dict]]:
+    # Loopback-only always-on backend (serve --isolated, never gated). Path is a parameter
+    # (CONTROL_READ_PATHS); same exemption class as _http_get for the session-token route scanner.
     token, _nonce = aod.ensure_credentials()
     started = time.monotonic()
     request = urllib.request.Request(f"http://127.0.0.1:{int(port)}{path}",
diff --git a/tests/hermes_cli/test_dashboard_session_token_routes.py b/tests/hermes_cli/test_dashboard_session_token_routes.py
index efa8f24aaf..01302316e6 100644
--- a/tests/hermes_cli/test_dashboard_session_token_routes.py
+++ b/tests/hermes_cli/test_dashboard_session_token_routes.py
@@ -114,6 +114,9 @@ _EXEMPT = {
     ("hermes_cli/always_on_rollover.py", "_http_post"):
         "roller -> its own loopback-only always-on backend (never gated); the path is a parameter "
         "(only /api/health/retirement, already a session-token route)",
+    ("hermes_cli/always_on_rollover.py", "_loopback_control_get"):
+        "superseded always-on backend -> the active successor on 127.0.0.1 (serve --isolated, never gated); "
+        "the path is a parameter because CONTROL_READ_PATHS is an allowlist, not a gated-dashboard route",
 }
 _API_PATH = re.compile(r"/api/[A-Za-z0-9_\-/{}.]*")
 
